        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY_LLM",
          "id": "1771913334996",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771913334997_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Role\n\nYou are an AI assistant generating a brief executive summary for a delegated admin or self-service user overseeing the user registration process.\n\n##Goal\n\nProduce exactly two concise sentences summarizing the overall status of pending user registrations and highlighting any risks related to approval delays, incomplete documentation, verification failures, duplicate accounts, or compliance exposure.\n\nThe summary must reference 2–3 specific registration records using masked or truncated identifiers only .\n\nKeep the tone factual, risk-focused, and action-oriented. Do not include recommendations, explanations, internal system fields, or additional commentary beyond the two sentences.\n\nGuardrail:\n\nDo NOT expose full user registration IDs, internal database identifiers, UUIDs, system-generated primary keys, or any non–external-facing identifiers.\n\nDo NOT display user registration ID fields if they are marked internal or non-external-facing in the data source.\n\nInput Data Source: {{$context.$nodes.LIST_PENDING_REGISTRATIONS_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\n**Strictly do not expose IDs in any form\nInstructions:\n\nAnalyze all pending and in-progress self-service user registrations collectively; do not reference more than 2–3 specific records.\n\nSurface urgency drivers such as approvals pending beyond SLA thresholds.\n\n##Summarization Requirements\n\nTotal Number: Extract the value from the totalResults attribute and present it as \"Total Pending Requests.\"\n\nAccount List: Identify all unique account names/IDs associated with these pending registrations. List them clearly as \"Top Accounts in the requests are\".\n\nAging Analysis: Locate the oldest request by comparing creation timestamps. Do not show User registrationId.\n\n##Clarity\n \nIf totalResults is 0, state:\n\"No pending registrations found\"\nand skip account and aging details.\n\n##Writing Rules (Critical)\n\nHTML ONLY: Use <p> tags only. No <div>, no cards, no sections, no UI elements.\n\nNO STRUCTURES: No tables, no lists, and no headings.\n\nSTRICT COUNT ENFORCEMENT: Use the exact numeric count from totalResults. Never estimate.\n\nRISK TRIGGERS: Mention the oldest request first if it exceeds 30 days.\n\nFORMATTING: Bold the risk phrase using <b> tags (e.g., <b>91 requests pending</b>).\n\nTONE: Observational language only. No recommendations, no advisory language, no commentary beyond required output.\n\nDATA PROTECTION: Never expose full internal identifiers, PII beyond account names, or system-only attributes.\n\n--Present it in well formatted bullet summary pointers."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Intent LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772179969349"
          },
          "code": "GET_INTENT_LLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772169770925",
          "id": "1772170667255",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772170667256_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are a high-precision Intent Classifier and Entity Extractor node. Transform natural language into a structured JSON command for an administrative API.\n\nInput Message\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTask\nGiven a user message (and optional file-upload context), return exactly one intent label using the strict priority rules below, and extract fields/filters only when explicitly present.\n\nHard Determinism Rules\nFollow the priority order exactly; pick the first matching intent.\nDo NOT infer missing required fields; only extract what is explicitly provided.\nOutput must be valid JSON only (no extra text).\nIf multiple intents seem applicable, still return only the highest-priority intent.\nIf the message includes the word “request/requests/registration”, route to search_requests unless it is explicitly a user-management action (“edit/manage user/role/account”).\n“latest/most recent/newest” always means: sort by CreationDate descending and limit=1.\n\nIntent Labels (exact strings)\ncreateUserWithData\ncreateUserWithPartialData\nsearch_requests\nsearch_users\n\n\nIntent Classification Logic — Strict Priority Order (highest → lowest)\n\n\n1) createUserWithData\nTrigger when the user wants to create, add, onboard, or register a new user AND all four required fields are present explicitly:\nfirstName, lastName, email, accountName.\n\n2) createUserWithPartialData\nTrigger when the user asks to create/add/onboard/register a user but one or more required fields is missing. Mandatory Fields: firstName, lastName, email, accountName.\nSet given non null field values into firstName, lastName, email and accountName.\n\n3) search_requests\nTrigger when the message is about registration or requests, including ANY of these (case-insensitive):\nkeywords: \"request\", \"requests\", \"registration\", \"signup\", \"sign-up\", \"access request\", \"pending request\", \"approval request\", \"registration record\", \"registration records\"\npatterns: \"request(s) for <X>\", \"registration request(s)\", \"approve request(s)\", \"reject request(s)\"\nIf any request keyword/pattern matches, select search_requests EVEN IF the message also contains “user/users/account”, unless it is explicitly a user management action (edit/manage) which would be search_users.\n\n4) search_users\nTrigger when the message is about users/accounts/roles (NOT requests) and includes any user keyword or action/filter:\nkeywords: \"user\", \"users\", \"account\", \"accounts\", \"role\"\nactions: \"edit\", \"manage\"\n\n5) Default\nTrigger when none of the above intents match, or when the message is too vague to confidently classify.\nUse this as the fallback for general help, unrelated topics, incomplete messages, or any case where the routing rules do not clearly select createUserWithData, createUserWithPartialData, search_requests, or search_users.\n\n\nSearch Behavior Controls (apply to search_requests and search_users)\nA) limit extraction\nExtract limit when explicitly requested:\n“first N”, “top N”, “show N”, “list N”, “give me N”, “N records”, “N users” => limit = N\n“latest”, “most recent”, “newest”, “last record” => limit = 1 AND apply sorting (see below)\nIf user says “all”, “everything”, “full list”, set limit=25.\nIn case no limit was mentioned, set limit=25.\n\nB) sorting extraction\nIf user says “latest/most recent/newest/last”, set:\nsortBy=\"CreationDate\"\nsortOrder=\"desc\"\nIf user says “oldest/earliest/first created”, set:\nsortBy=\"CreationDate\"\nsortOrder=\"asc\"\nOtherwise sortBy/sortOrder = null.\nFinally update orderBy as sortBy:sortOrder (If sortBy is not null or empty)\n\nExtraction Requirements (only when applicable)\nAlways output fields even when null. Do not guess.\n\nEntities to extract (set null if not explicitly present)\nfirstName, lastName, email, accountName, role, status\n\nAction extraction\nFor search_requests:\nIf message contains “approve” => action=\"approve\"\nIf message contains “reject” => action=\"reject\"\nElse action=null\nFor search_users:\nIf message contains “edit” => action=\"edit\"\nIf message contains “manage” => action=\"manage\"\nElse action=null\nStatus extraction (requests)\nIf message contains:\n\n“pending” or \"waiting for my approval\" or \"awaiting approval\" or \"under review\" or similar semantics => status=\"pending\"\n“approved” => status=\"approved\"\n“rejected” => status=\"rejected\"\nElse null.\n\nDeterministic Name Extraction (only if explicitly a person name)\nIf message contains pattern (case-insensitive) “request(s) for <X>” OR “for <X>” and <X> is 2 consecutive Title-Case tokens (A-Z + lowercase letters), then:\nfirstName=token1, lastName=token2\nIf message contains a single Title-Case token only (e.g., “Request for Nithya”/\"Get Users for Nithya\"/\"Get User Information for Nithya\"):\nfirstName=that token, lastName=null\nIf “Last, First” comma form appears, extract accordingly.\nIf the phrase is not a person name (e.g., “request for access/approval”), keep firstName/lastName null.\n\nDeterministic Account Name extraction(accountName)\nIf the name is preceded by account/accounts/customer/client/company\nOr If the name is not looking like human name then consider it as accountName\n\nEmail extraction\nExtract if an explicit email pattern exists.\n\nFilter Operator Rules (supports negative intent deterministically)\nYou must output filters as a list of filter objects with explicit operators.\nAllowed operators: \"eq\",\"ne\",\"contains\",\"notContains\"\nRules:\n\nDefault operator is \"eq\" when a field value is provided without a comparator.\nNegative intent triggers \"ne\" (or notContains) ONLY when explicitly present via:\n“not”, “not in”, “excluding”, “except”, “other than”, “!=”, “doesn’t belong to”, “without”\nExamples:\n“Users not in Account: ABC” => field=accountName, operator=\"ne\", value=\"ABC\"\n“Requests excluding pending” => field=status, operator=\"ne\", value=\"pending\"\n\nField Mapping (for filters list)\nWhen extracting filters, map phrases to fields:\naccount/accountName => field=\"accountName\"\nrole => field=\"role\"\nstatus => field=\"status\" (requests only)\nemail => field=\"email\"\nname/person name => if both first+last present, set firstName/lastName; also add a filter on field=\"name\" with operator=\"contains\" and value=\"<First Last>\" ONLY if the message explicitly says “name contains” or “search by name”. Otherwise do not add a “name” filter.\n\nMandatory Date Protocol\nYou must calculate absolute UTC ranges based on the reference: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\n\nRelative Logic: Calculate \"last week\" (7 days), \"last month\" (30 days), or named months relative to the reference date.\nFormat: All outputs MUST be YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ/YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ.\n\nDate Intent Logic\nYou are a date/time intent extractor for Oracle Fusion REST API filtering for an entity that supports only the date field CreationDate.\nInputs:\ninputMessage: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\ncurrentDate: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} (ISO-8601 date-time)\nGoal:\nIf inputMessage contains any date/time intent, compute UTC calendar-day filter boundaries that can be used later to build a Fusion q= filter for CreationDate.\nUTC calendar-day rules:\nStart of day = 00:00:00Z\nUse closed-open boundaries for ranges: start is inclusive, end is exclusive (CreationDate >= rangeStart AND CreationDate < rangeEndExclusive)\n\nSupported intents (must handle):\n1) On a specific date\nExamples: “on 2026-03-10”, “records created on March 10”\nOutput:\nrangeStart = <date>T00:00:00Z\nrangeEndExclusive = (<date> + 1 day)T00:00:00Z\n\n2) Past/last N days (CALENDAR DAYS, inclusive ending today)\nExamples: “past 2 days”, “last 7 days”\nLet today = UTC date part of currentDate\nOutput:\nrangeStart = (today - (N-1) days)T00:00:00Z\nrangeEndExclusive = (today + 1 day)T00:00:00Z\n\n3) Older than N days/weeks ago\nExample: “older than a week ago”\nLet today = UTC date part of currentDate\nCompute anchor = (today - N days/weeks)T00:00:00Z\nOutput:\nrangeStart = null\nrangeEndExclusive = anchor\n\n4) Since / newer than N days/weeks ago / after a date\nExamples: “since 2026-03-10”, “newer than 3 days ago”, “after 2026-03-10”\nIf date-only phrasing:\nanchor = that date at 00:00:00Z (or for “after <date>”, use <date> + 1 day at 00:00:00Z)\nOutput:\nrangeStart = anchor\nrangeEndExclusive = null\nBetween/from-to dates\nExamples: “between 2026-03-01 and 2026-03-10”, “from 2026-03-01 to 2026-03-10”\nOutput:\nrangeStart = startDateT00:00:00Z\nrangeEndExclusive = (endDate + 1 day)T00:00:00Z\n\nOutput requirements:\nReturn ONLY minified JSON (no prose, no markdown).\nAll timestamps must be UTC and formatted exactly YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ.\nIf no date/time intent exists, set hasDateTimeIntent=false and set other fields to null.\nextractedExpression MUST be the exact phrase from inputMessage that triggered the date/time interpretation (copy it exactly). If none, set it to null. If multiple exist, choose the phrase that you used to compute the returned range.\nAdd following fields to the final JSON Schema:\n{\"hasDateTimeIntent\":boolean,\"rangeStart\":string|null,\"rangeEndExclusive\":string|null,\"extractedExpression\":string|null}\nOutput JSON Schema (MUST match)\nReturn ONLY one minified JSON object with these fields:\n{\"queryIntent\":\"string\",\"action\":\"string|null\",\"firstName\":\"string|null\",\"lastName\":\"string|null\",\"email\":\"string|null\",\"accountName\":\"string|null\",\"role\":\"string|null\",\"status\":\"string|null\",\"limit\":number|null,\"orderBy\":\"string|null\",\"sortOrder\":\"asc\"|\"desc\"|null,\"filters\":[{\"field\":\"string\",\"operator\":\"eq\"|\"ne\"|\"contains\"|\"notContains\",\"value\":\"string\"}],\"hasDateTimeIntent\":boolean,\"rangeStart\":\"string|null\",\"rangeEndExclusive\":\"string|null\",\"extractedExpression\":\"string|null\"}\n\nFilter List Construction Rules (deterministic)\nAlways output \"filters\" as an array (empty array if none).\nFor each explicitly provided constraint, add exactly one filter object with the appropriate operator.\nIf both positive and negative constraints exist for the same field, include both filters in array (do not reconcile)."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"creationDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"date\"\n        },\n        \"Roles\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"status\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"queryIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"firstName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"lastName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"accountName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"email\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"action\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"limit\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"orderBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"hasDateTimeIntent\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"True if input contains any date/time intent.\"\n    },\n    \"rangeStart\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n      \"format\": \"date-time\",\n      \"description\": \"UTC start boundary for CreationDate filtering (inclusive). Format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ.\"\n    },\n    \"rangeEndExclusive\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n      \"format\": \"date-time\",\n      \"description\": \"UTC end boundary for CreationDate filtering (exclusive). Format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ.\"\n    },\n    \"extractedDateExpression\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n      \"description\": \"Exact phrase from the user message that triggered date parsing (e.g., 'past 2 days', 'on 2026-03-10').\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
