          "code": "LIST_SS_USERS_LLM_AC",
          "id": "1771525357330",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771525357331_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "System Input: Use the list available at: {{$context.$nodes.LIST_SS_USERS_AC.$output}}\n\n## STRICT RULES\n- Always generate <ActionId based on userId and AccountPartyID.\n- ora.Invoke should always be in format ora.Invoke(\"GetRoles\", GetRoles <ActionId>)\n- Strictly show the defined summary always and do not include any heading\n- Do not duplicate the title\n\nInstructions:\n- Set the panel title to \"Self-Service Users\"\n- Strictly Show the  panel description/Summary as `There are <totalCount> self-service users. The 5 most recently updated are displayed below - refine your search (for example, by name or email) to see details for the right user.`\n- Use the value for <totalCount> from {{$context.$nodes.LIST_SS_USERS_AC.$output.totalResults}}\n- Show the exact text defined as description/summary always\n\n\n##Table Display: Render a table with the following columns:\n 1. Name\n 2. Email\n 3. Roles\n 4. Account\n 5. Action ( leave column label blank, containing the button).\n\n##Transformation & Logic:\n 1. ActionId Mapping: For each item in the list, derive an ActionId by concatenating userId and AccountPartyId (Format: UserId,AccountPartyId).\n 2. Button Logic: Every row must include a button labeled \"Edit Roles\".\n 3. Function Call: Set the button's action property to: ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", GetRoles <ActionId>), replacing <ActionId> with the value derived in Step 1."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Action",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const invokedAction = $context?.$app?.$OraAction || \"\";\n// Split and filter out extra spaces\n// Split safely\nconst [action = null, contextId = null, name = null] = invokedAction.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n\nreturn { action, contextId, name };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771579149566"
          },
