          "code": "SEARCH_REGISTRATION_REQUESTS_LLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775814266322",
          "id": "1774290636808",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774290636809_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "System Input: {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_REQUESTS_BO.$output}}\n\nStrict Data Rules:\n\nUse ONLY values explicitly present in the input JSON.\nDO NOT infer, estimate, calculate, or fabricate any field.\nIf a required field is missing, return null or 0 instead of guessing.\nNever create totals, statuses, or dates that are not in the payload.\nTreat the input JSON as the single source of truth.\nNever invent additional orders.\n\n\nInstructions:\n# Handling No Records:\nIn case of no Records in the System Input. Generate a polite response indicating no records with the requested Criteria and user can check with different search criteria and Terminate. Don't prompt any other information.\n\n#Handling Input.\nNormalize the input into a list of registrations (do not filter only pending; include whatever records are returned).\nSet Panel Title to \"Registration Requests\".\nAge calculation rules:\ncurrent time: {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\ncreation time: item.CreationDate\nCompute each item's age.\nOldest request age = age of the earliest CreationDate.\nDisplay age in hours if < 24 hours, otherwise in days (rounded down is fine).\n\nSummary generation (status-aware):\nDetermine whether returned records are all Pending, all Approved, all Rejected, or Mixed (based only on the status values present in the payload).\nIf all Pending: show a pending-focused summary like:\n\"There are X registration requests pending approval, with the oldest submitted Y days ago. Here are the most recent requests for you to review and approve.\"\nIf all Approved: summarize approved records:\nIf hasMore=\"false from the System Input, show \"There are X approved registration requests in the system{{datePhrase}}.\". If hasMore=\"true\" from System Input, show \"Following are the approved registration requests {{datePhrase}}.\"\nIf all Rejected: summarize rejected records:\nIf hasMore=\"false from the System Input, show \"There are X rejected registration requests in the system{{datePhrase}}.\". If hasMore=\"true\" from System Input, show \"Following are the rejected registration requests {{datePhrase}}.\"\nIf Mixed: summarize total and include a simple breakdown by status (Pending/Approved/Rejected counts), using only statuses present in the payload.\n\nDate phrase rule:\nBased on {{$context.$variables.extractedExpression}}, append datePhrase = \" from the last Z days\" ONLY if Z is explicitly available from upstream context (e.g., an extracted user phrase such as “past 7 days” provided to you). If Z is not explicitly provided, omit the datePhrase entirely. Do not invent Z. \n\nItem rendering rules:\nbadgeText must reflect each item’s actual status from the payload (do not force “Pending”).\nIf registrationId (or equivalent id field used in the command) is missing for an item, set followUpCommand and AddditionalAction to null for that item (do not fabricate an id).\n\nOutput Format (one object per registration record):\n{\n\"title\": \"FirstName LastName\",\n\"subtitle\": \"AccountName\",\n\"summary\": \"Email address\",\n\"badgeText\": \"Status\",\n\"priority\": \"medium\",\n\"timestamp\": \"Submitted <X> days/hours ago\",\n\"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\",Review <registrationId>)\",\n\"AddditionalAction\": \"ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\",Review <registrationId>)\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
