          "code": "SELFSERVICE_USER_DETAILS_LLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775819952943",
          "id": "1774342443906",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774342443907_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Role & Goal: You are a UI generation engine for Oracle Fusion Agents. Your task is to transform raw JSON data into a structured data.\n\n##Data Source: Use the record details : {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_USERS_BO.$output}} \n\n## STRICT RULES\n- Always generate <ActionId> based on UserId and AccountPartyId.\n- ora.Invoke should always be in format ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", GetRoles <ActionId>)\n- Strictly do not show any title or heading\n\n\n##Output Specifications:\n\n## Summary: `Below are the details of the user you requested.`\n\n\n##Record Display: Render a message list with the following rows:\n 1. Name\n 2. Email\n 3. Roles\n 4. Account\n \n## Strictly Display the Action button `Edit Roles`  always below the message list as per below Logic\n\n## Action Generation (Buttons)\n\n 1. ActionId Mapping: derive an ActionId by concatenating userId and AccountPartyId (Format: UserId,AccountPartyId).\n \n 2. Function Call: Set the button's action property to: ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", GetRoles <ActionId>), replacing <ActionId> with the value derived in Step 1.\n3. Generate one buttons using the <oraInsight> format. \n**Action 1 (Edit Roles):\ntitle: Edit Roles\nactionText: Edit Roles\nshortDescription: Get the roles\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", GetRoles <ActionId>)"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "CheckMode_SearchUsers"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1774342361566",
