          "code": "SELFSERVICE_USERS_SEARCH_RESULTS_LLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775820078708",
          "id": "1774342361566",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774342361567_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "System Input: {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_USERS_BO.$output}} \n\nStrict Data Rules:\n\nUse ONLY values explicitly present in the input JSON.\nDO NOT infer, estimate, calculate, or fabricate any field.\nIf a required field is missing, return null or 0 instead of guessing.\nNever create totals, statuses, or dates that are not in the payload.\nTreat the input JSON as the single source of truth.\nNever invent additional orders.\n\nInstructions:\n# Handling No Records:\nIf the System Input contains zero user records (e.g., the records array is missing, null, or empty; OR totalResults/count is 0), output `No user records found for the given criteria'. AND TERMINATE and nothing else. Do not render any table header, columns, buttons, titles, or additional text. Do not execute any next steps.\n\n#Handling Input.\nNormalize the input into a list of users multi-record widget(do not filter only pending; include whatever records are returned).\nSet Panel Title to \"Self-Service Users\".\nStrictly Show the Panel Description/Summary text always as \"There are {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_USERS_BO.$output.count}}  self-service users.\"\nStrictly do not add any other sentences before or after this text.\n\n##Table Display: Render a table with the following columns:\n 1. Name\n 2. Email\n 3. Roles\n 4. Account\n 5. Action ( leave column label blank, containing the button).\n\n##Transformation & Logic:\n 1. ActionId Mapping: For each item in the list, derive an ActionId by concatenating userId and AccountPartyId (Format: UserId,AccountPartyId).\n 2. Button Logic: Every row must include a button labeled \"Edit Roles\" always.\n 3. Function Call: Set the button's action property to: ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", GetRoles <ActionId>), replacing <ActionId> with the value derived in Step 1.\n\n##Formatting Constraints:\n 1. Do NOT include a title for the table itself.\n2. Do NOT show any badges"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
